Subject: [PATCH 0081] macOS-side diagnostics: GPU and boot-framebuffer power/events, flight log synced per step

Wildcat Lake: with the firmware's boot framebuffer still on the GPU, NMXGPU's framebuffer registering its power
driver froze the Mac within milliseconds (test 23); retiring the boot framebuffer froze it (test 21) or, done before
xe took the GPU, panicked in IOFramebuffer::terminate (NULL+0x120, test 24); with neither (test 22) the Mac ran on
but IOGraphics never opened the new framebuffer. The flight recorder's 40 ms writes missed the last steps.

- xnu/nmx_kext.cpp (nmxtrace): before the publish, NMXGPU registers as an interested driver for power changes of the
  GPU's PCI device and of IONDRVFramebuffer, for IOGraphics' events of IONDRVFramebuffer, and for IOKit messages to
  both; each is an "attach:" breadcrumb with the PCI command register and D-state (from the PM capability).
- xnu/nmx_flight.cpp: nmx_flight_sync() writes and syncs the ring on the caller's thread (a lock shared with the
  writer thread); bsdcompat/src/nmx_trace.c calls it after each NMXGPU breadcrumb.

Applies on top of 0051-0080.

